Anna Brown is a 26-year-old female with a past medical history significant for epilepsy, depression, and peptic ulcer disease who presents with left elbow pain.

The patient is a right-handed office worker who reports that she sits at her desk all day and types. She states that she has been experiencing left elbow pain. She notes that the pain is stiff and swollen, and she is having difficulty opening and closing her left elbow. She denies any numbness or tingling in her hands or weakness in her arm. She reports that she can still write with her right hand, which is good.

The patient reports that she has not had any seizures in the past year. She is still taking Keppra. She reports that she is doing well with therapy and is still avoiding medication for her depression. She denies any active suicidal or homicidal ideation.

The patient reports that she has been doing well with her peptic ulcer disease since her endoscopy. She denies fever or chills.

REVIEW OF SYSTEMS

• Constitutional: Denies fever or chills.
• Musculoskeletal: Reports left elbow pain.
