HISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS

Ms. Johnson is a 31-year-old female with a past medical history of type 2 diabetes and hypertension who presents with abnormal lab findings.

The patient reports that she has been feeling tired, lacking a lot of energy, and has had swollen joints in her elbows, which really hurts. She has been having body aches. She notes that she has been feeling a little nauseous and has not been able to eat much, just keeping to toast and crackers. She has been trying to stay away from salty foods. She notes that she has had some other rash elsewhere. She had an insect bite a couple of weeks ago. She denies any high fevers.

Regarding her diabetes, she states that her blood sugars have been okay, especially with the acute illness. She is currently taking metformin. She has been monitoring her blood sugars at home and they have been within a range.

Regarding her hypertension, she is still taking lisinopril. She has been monitoring her blood pressures at home, and they have been okay. She is staying away from salty foods.

Ms. Johnson endorses nausea, joint pain, and body aches.

