• Integumentary: Bull's-eye rash on the left abdomen. Warm to palpation. No tenderness to palpation. No erythema or cellulitis.

RESULTS

Lyme titer is elevated.

Lyme Western Blot: Positive.

Labs: WBC, CMP, and CBC are within normal limits.

