She states she has been using her Wixela 250/50 dose once in the morning and once at night and has not had any issues with it. She rarely uses her albuterol inhaler and only does so before strenuous activity. She is trying to use her daily inhaler less because she is trying to get into the military soon.

The patient denies any urgent care or ER visits for breathing over the past year. She has not been on prednisone for breathing issues.

Regarding her allergies, she uses Zyrtec as needed during the spring and fall. She denies any issues with her daily use of Zyrtec during the spring.

The patient states that she has been cautious since her last encounter and wears long sleeves and changes gloves when cleaning cars. She has an epipen that she keeps with her.

Regarding her tree nut allergy, she states that she has had some testing previously and tolerates almonds and cashews.

PAST HISTORY

Medical
Asthma
Allergic rhinitis
Peanut allergy

SOCIAL HISTORY

The patient works outside 3 days a week.

MEDICATIONS

Albuterol inhaler as needed.
Zyrtec as needed in the spring, summer, and fall.
Wixela 250/50 once in the morning and once at night.

