Asthma.
• Medical Reasoning: The patient's asthma score is 21. She is currently using Wixela 250/50 once in the morning and once at night and is doing well. She rarely uses her albuterol inhaler. She has a history of smoking and vaping but is trying to cut back. She has been switched from Symbicort to Wixela due to insurance changes.
• Patient Education and Counseling: We discussed the asthma regimen and that it is a stepwise process. We also discussed the benefits of minimizing her inhaler use unless she is ill or during smoke season. We discussed the possibility of stepping down to an inhaler with one medication in it, which is covered by her insurance.
• Medical Treatment: Continue Wixela 250/50 once in the morning and once at night. We will repeat her spirometry in 4 months. We will also document her breathing tests for the military. I will call in Alvesco 80 mcg, 2 puffs twice a day, and renew her albuterol and epipen.

Allergic rhinitis.
• Medical Reasoning: The patient uses Zyrtec as needed in the spring, summer, and fall and reports it works well.
