• Medical Treatment: Continue Zyrtec 10 mg as needed.

Peanut allergy.
• Medical Reasoning: The patient has a known peanut allergy and tolerates almonds and cashews.
• Patient Education and Counseling: She should continue to avoid peanuts and tree nuts.
• Medical Treatment: Continue to avoid peanuts and tree nuts. She has an epipen that she keeps with her.

Patient Agreements: The patient understands and agrees with the recommended medical treatment plan.

INSTRUCTIONS

The patient will follow-up in 4 months with ACT and spirometry, sooner if needed. }}<|eot_id|>
