Scott Harris is a 45-year-old male who presents to the clinic today for the evaluation of right knee pain. The onset of his pain began 3 days ago. The patient states he was playing soccer over the weekend and felt a pop in his right knee. He reports that he has swelling in the knee, but it has decreased since onset. The patient states that his knee is swollen and stiff, and he has been unable to fully extend or flex his right knee. He denies taking anything for pain other than anti-inflammatory medications. He is able to bear weight on the right leg but reports that it feels loose.

REVIEW OF SYSTEMS

Musculoskeletal: Reports right knee pain, swelling, and decreased range of motion.
Skin: Reports ecchymosis.

