The patient is a 52-year-old female who presents to the clinic today for the evaluation of elbow pain. She states that she has been experiencing moderate to severe pain on the medial aspect of her elbow for the past 4 days. The pain radiates down her arm and along the medial aspect of her arm. She denies any history of elbow injuries. The patient states that she has been doing pottery and making a ceramic bowl for her son’s birthday. She is unable to continue working on the pottery due to the pain. She reports that the pain wakes her up at night. She denies using any medications to relieve the pain. She has tried ice and ibuprofen with no relief.

The patient has a history of hypertension and diabetes mellitus type 2. She is currently taking lisinopril 10 mg and metformin 500 mg twice daily. She states that she takes her medications regularly and has been compliant with dietary recommendations. She notes that her blood pressure has been in the teens to thirties over the past few weeks. She reports that she checks her blood pressure regularly.

The patient also enjoys baking and making cinnamon rolls. She states that she sometimes forgets to take her medications due to her busy schedule. She notes that she has a sweet tooth and her blood sugars have been a little higher over the past few weeks. She reports that she has been walking daily for about 1-2 miles in the morning and evening.

ROS:

• Musculoskeletal: Reports moderate to severe pain on the medial aspect of her elbow. Denies any history of elbow injuries.
• General: Reports that she is unable to continue working on pottery due to the pain. Reports that she is awakened by the pain at night.

Vital Signs:
• Blood pressure: 120/70 mmHg
• Respiratory rate: 18
• Temperature: 97.9°F
• Pulse: 78

Physical Exam:
• Musculoskeletal: Moderate tenderness to palpation on the medial epicondyle of the right elbow. Pain with resisted pronation of the right forearm. Pain with flexion and extension of the wrist.

Impression:

1. Right elbow pain.
2. Hypertension.
3. Diabetes mellitus type 2.

Plan:

1. Right elbow pain.
   • Medical treatment: Rest, sling to be worn while awake, ice to the elbow for 20 minutes 3 times a day, ibuprofen 600 mg (3 tablets) every 6 hours with food for 1 week.
