At this point, I discussed the diagnosis and treatment options with the patient. I recommended that he keep his leg elevated and ice it. I recommended that he be given an Aircast to help stabilize the ankle. I also recommended that he be given crutches for the next 1 to 2 days and then he may start walking on it as tolerated. The patient was also advised to continue to take NSAIDs as needed to help with the pain. All questions were answered.

